## Memory protocol

Everything needed to resume lives on disk in `.copilot/test-ledger/`, never in
the conversation.

```json
{
  "schema": "react-unit-test-engineering/progress@1",
  "updatedAt": "2026-09-04T11:42:00.000Z",
  "runner": "vitest",
  "baseline": { "tests": 412, "failing": 3, "statements": 71.4, "branches": 58.2 },
  "gates": { "coverage": 100, "mutationScore": 100, "maxSurvivors": 0 },
  "pending": [
    { "target": "src/components/UserCard.tsx", "reason": "no importing test" }
  ],
  "inProgress": {
    "target": "src/components/DataTable.tsx",
    "phase": "mutation",
    "note": "3 survivors on the sort comparator, lines 88-96"
  },
  "done": [
    {
      "target": "src/components/Button.tsx",
      "testFile": "src/components/Button.test.tsx",
      "casesAdded": 11,
      "coverage": { "statements": 100, "branches": 100, "functions": 100 },
      "mutationScore": 100
    }
  ],
  "blocked": [
    {
      "target": "src/legacy/ChartCanvas.tsx",
      "reason": "requires a real canvas context; needs a user decision on jsdom-canvas"
    }
  ],
  "inheritedFailures": ["src/hooks/useSession.test.ts > refreshes the token before expiry"]
}
```

Rules:

- `inProgress` holds **at most one** target. Two means an earlier run died
  without checkpointing — verify that target's real state with the tools before
  trusting the note.
- Nothing moves to `done` until every gate passed in a command you actually ran
  this session.
- `blocked` is not failure. It is the right destination for anything needing a
  human decision, and it is what you report at the end.
- `inheritedFailures` is written once, at baseline, and never edited to make
  progress look better.

`conventions.md` is append-only prose — every fact about *this* repo that cost a
tool call to learn, so future sessions do not pay again:

```markdown
# Repo testing conventions
- Runner: Vitest 3.2.4, environment jsdom, setup file `src/test-setup.ts`.
- RTL 16.x with user-event 14.x — always `const user = userEvent.setup()`.
- Tests co-located: `Component.tsx` + `Component.test.tsx`.
- Components under `src/features/**` need `renderWithProviders` from `src/test-utils/render.tsx`.
- MSW handlers in `src/mocks/handlers.ts`; server starts in the setup file.
- `IntersectionObserver` is not in jsdom; polyfilled in `src/test-setup.ts`.
- Path alias `@/` -> `src/`, declared in both tsconfig and vite.config.ts.
```

**Context budgeting.** The failure mode on a large job is loading too much and
losing the thread:

- One module at a time. Read the target and its existing test file. Do not read
  sibling components "for context" — the inventory already says what exists.
- Prefer tool output to file contents. Four lines of coverage gap beat the HTML
  report.
- Truncate loops: after three coverage/mutation iterations on one module,
  checkpoint, move it to `blocked` with the specific obstacle, and continue.
- After finishing a module, the only things surviving into the next are its
  `done` entry and any new line in `conventions.md`.

**Resume procedure.** Read `progress.json` and `conventions.md` — nothing else
yet. Re-run the inventory grep; the working tree may have moved. If `inProgress`
is set, verify its real state before trusting the note. Continue from the first
failing gate — never restart a module from Phase 3 if its tests already exist,
because that is how duplicates get created. If git HEAD contradicts the ledger
(test files vanished, targets renamed), say so and re-plan.

