## Network timeouts and retries

**Retry the network. Never retry a test.** A transient network failure is noise;
a failing test is information. Retrying the second converts a reproducible
defect into an intermittent one.

Wrap every network-touching command:

```bash
retry() {  # retry <attempts> <timeout-seconds> -- <command...>
  local attempts=$1 timeout_s=$2; shift 3
  local n=1 delay=2 code=0
  until timeout --signal=TERM --kill-after=10s "${timeout_s}s" "$@"; do
    code=$?
    if [ $n -ge "$attempts" ]; then
      echo "retry: exhausted $attempts attempts (last exit $code)" >&2; return $code
    fi
    # 124 = timed out; 7/128/137/143 = unavailable or killed. Anything else is
    # a real failure and must not be retried.
    case $code in
      124|7|128|137|143) ;;
      *) echo "retry: exit $code is a REAL failure, not retrying" >&2; return $code ;;
    esac
    echo "retry: transient failure (exit $code), attempt $n/$attempts, backing off ${delay}s" >&2
    sleep $delay; delay=$((delay * 2)); n=$((n + 1))
  done
}

# Make npm resilient before the wrapper ever has to retry the whole command.
export npm_config_fetch_retries=5
export npm_config_fetch_retry_maxtimeout=120000
export npm_config_fetch_timeout=300000

retry 4 600 -- npm ci
retry 3 2400 -- npx stryker run
```

Budgets: `npm ci` 10 min × 4; full `vitest run` 15 min × 2; a single test file
2 min × 1 (no network in it, so any failure is real); full `stryker run` 40 min
× 3.

Behind a corporate proxy, verify the environment before blaming the tooling —
`npm config get registry proxy https-proxy strict-ssl` and
`echo "$HTTP_PROXY $HTTPS_PROXY $NO_PROXY"`. Never disable `strict-ssl`, never
switch registries, never hardcode a proxy. If the registry is unreachable,
report it and stop.

**Flakes have five causes, all fixable:** an unawaited state update (the
`act(...)` warning — `await` the user-event call or use `findBy*`); real timers
(fake them, wiring `advanceTimers` into `userEvent.setup()`); a shared mutable
fixture (build fixtures inside the test); an unmocked request (set MSW's
`onUnhandledRequest: 'error'`); order dependence (reproduce with
`npx vitest run --sequence.shuffle`, then fix the leaked global). Forbidden
"fixes": `retry: 2` in config, a longer `waitFor` timeout, an added sleep,
`it.skip`.

